  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 01f934d50526431a9392a6ceca1dc33d, type: 3}
  m_Name: Rampage Cell Config 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  CellName: Rampage
  Description: Demolition arena cell, intensity 1 of 4 - a quiet arena you have mostly to yourself: 59
    seeded plants totalling ~9830 prisms of cacti, spires, pines, rosettes and coral,
    filling the volume from just outside the nucleus out to the membrane, across all three
    domains, each plant one of the four elemental variations. The PLANT AND PRISM COUNTS ARE
    THE SAME AT EVERY INTENSITY - what intensity changes is how BIG things are and how
    contested they get: prisms at 1.6x the authored leaf (bigger is an easier target for the
    cone and an easier surface to skim), a nucleus at prefab scale 500 (~490u radius), 1x
    the authored wildlife, and - authored in the scene, not here - twice as many crystals as
    players. Intensity 4 is the shipped, play-tested arena exactly; 1 is the same arena made
    bigger and easier to hit. The nucleus stays clear (the planting band is clamped outside
    it) and is the crystals' contested ground. The mature forest is ~1,530,311 volume, and
    this cell's VOLUME thresholds are the play-tested intensity-4 ladder scaled by that - so
    Frenzy sits the same 4.11x above the forest at every level. Pending an in-editor
    re-measure; regenerate with Tools/Build/rampage_intensity.py rather than hand-editing.
